Question 1: Types of Operators in JavaScript

1. Arithmetic Operators (Used for math operations)  
  
   let a = 10, b = 5;
   console.log(a + b); 
   console.log(a % b); 

   
2. Assignment Operators --(Assign values to variables)  
 
   let x = 10;
   x += 5; // x = x + 5
   console.log(x); // 15
   ```

3. Comparison Operators (Compare values)  
  
   console.log(5 == "5"); 
   console.log(5 === "5"); 
  

4. Logical Operators(Used for conditions)  
  
   console.log(true && false); 
   console.log(true || false); /
   console.log(!true);        



Question 2: Difference Between `==` and `===` 

- `==` (Loose comparison) → Compares only values, ignores types.  

  console.log(5 == "5"); 

`===` (Strict comparison) → Compares values and types.  
  console.log(5 === "5");

